      "message": "As far as I can see, the only observer that needs this is the `LazyFree` read in madvise_free_p3s.c (aosp/4367986): folio_mark_lazyfree() leaves small folios in the per-CPU `lru_lazyfree` batch (see folio_may_be_lru_cached()), and smaps counts a folio as `LazyFree` only once lru_lazyfree() has cleared `PG_swapbacked`.\n\nSmall folios in native processes behave the same, and upstream doesn\u0027t drain here. The P3S sibling fault path doesn\u0027t need it either, since p3s_anon_folio_unreferenced() drains for itself.\n\nWould it be OK to drop the drain and let the test flush the batch instead? For example, it could pin itself to one CPU and call `madvise(MADV_COLD)` on a scratch page before reading smaps, since madvise_cold() starts with lru_add_drain().",
